#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Definition]
#title[Type of Surjective Cartesian Decompositions]

Let $S : "FinSet"$. We define the species of _surjective cartesian decompositions_ by
$
  "surj-cart-dec" (S) :-= sum_(A,B : "FinSet")(A xx_"FinSet" B  ~= S) xx "is-surj"(pi_1) xx "is-surj"(pi_2).
$
Where $xx_"FinSet"$ is the #local("00DZ")[cartesian product in FinSet].
$pi_1 : A xx B -> A$ and $pi_2 : A xx B -> B$ are the projections onto the first and second factor respectively.
In #local("00I2")[agda unimath] this type is called `binary-surjective-product-Decomposition`.
